semantics(ead2a54f) {
  name: "core"
  scope: always
  paths: []
  cues: []
  holds: """
    Replace this first line during /adopt-holon with a one-line summary of the project's packages, targets and products. Paths are relative to the project root folder.
    Replies to the user are prose; plans, tasks, memories, questions and issues are closures filed through .agents/harness/bin/write.
    Commits and pushes in this repository are the user's; write done ticks a task and commits nothing.
    The code wins over any doc; a doc that disagrees with the code is the thing to fix.
    Scripts and hooks under .agents/harness/ are single Swift files; the harness uses no Python.
    Project files change through .agents/harness/bin/edit; the built-in Edit and Write tools are refused on project files.
    Find code with .agents/harness/bin/seek TERM [PATH…], not grep: it returns whole units as FILE:A-B plus a hash for edit --range.
    """
  terms: """
    record: a closure under .agents/records/, written only through bin/write
    view: a generated .md beside the records, never edited by hand
    semantics card: one record in records/SEMANTICS/; this core card rides with every injection
    """
  next: """
    .agents/ATLAS.md: finding the one detail file for a path or task
    .agents/harness/rules/GROK.md: writing any reply or doc
    .agents/records/TODO.md: open work
    .agents/harness/rules/EDITING.md: changing a project file with the edit tool
    """
}
